<section id="terminal-ui" class="terminal-section" aria-labelledby="terminal-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">New in 0.11.0 · Ready to use</p>
  <h2 id="terminal-heading">A complete authenticator, inside your terminal.</h2>
  <p>Create a vault, add your first account and manage your codes through forms. No command syntax to remember for everyday account and vault operations.</p>
  <div class="ui-benefits">
    <article><span class="step-label">01 / ACCOUNTS</span><h3>From setup key to live code</h3><p>Add manually or paste a masked provisioning URI. Search, rename and remove accounts from the same dashboard.</p></article>
    <article><span class="step-label">02 / TIMING</span><h3>Know how long you have</h3><p>Codes refresh automatically. A countdown and validity bar follow each account’s actual period. Copy only when you choose.</p></article>
    <article><span class="step-label">03 / YOUR VAULT</span><h3>Back up. Export. Lock.</h3><p>Create encrypted copies, import a D2FA vault or change its password. Lock with Ctrl+L; five minutes without input locks the session too.</p></article>
  </div>
  <div class="launch-strip"><div><h3>Open the UI</h3><p>Start locked, then unlock or create your vault.</p></div><pre><code>d2fa ui</code></pre></div>
  <p class="muted">Writes, backup and export ask for your password again. This is a terminal interface for Windows, macOS and Linux. Prefer scripts? All CLI commands remain available.</p>
  <p><a href="/docs/cli#terminal-ui">UI guide and keyboard shortcuts →</a></p>
</section>
